---
description: Run the ui-design-review skill on any React UI you create or change before reporting the work as done
globs: **/*.tsx,**/*.jsx,**/*.css,**/*.scss
alwaysApply: false
---

When you create or modify user-facing React UI (components, pages, layouts,
styles), you are not finished when the code compiles. Before reporting the
work as done:

1. Use the `ui-design-review` skill: capture the affected view(s) with
   Playwright, run the source scan, and look at the screenshots.
2. Fix critical and major findings, using the corporate components and tokens
   described in `.cursor/skills/ui-design-review/design-system/`.
3. Re-capture to confirm, and include the before → after counts plus anything
   left for a human decision in your summary.

Skip this only for changes with no visual or interaction effect (types, tests,
data plumbing), and say that you skipped it.
